# Our libraries, developed alongside postcards

postcards is the first big user of a family of our own young libraries. They
sit next to it on disk and in the workspace, and postcards depends on them by
path, never by registry version or git URL:

| Library | Path | What it gives postcards |
|---|---|---|
| penfill | `../penfill` | pen fills (patterns) inside polygons |
| terramask | `../terramask` | sea, land, landcover, parks as polygons from vector tiles; elevation and depth bands from terrain tiles |
| burin-map | `../burin-map` | pen-and-ink terrain drawing (formerly VectorsMap); uses terramask itself |

Strategy:

- When postcards needs something a library should own, change the library
  rather than working around it in postcards. Same for bugs found there.
- Before writing geometry or tile code in postcards, check whether one of
  them already does it (terramask for anything from map or terrain tiles).
- Keep them on one copy: libraries that depend on each other do so by path
  too (burin-map reads `../terramask`), with `version` kept next to `path`
  where the crate is published.
- After changing a library, build and test it in its own repo, then rebuild
  postcards (and `web/build-wasm.sh` when the WASM side is affected).
